<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/optical-sensors">Optical &amp; Sensors</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">MEMS Sensors</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Optical &amp; Sensors products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/optical-sensors/camera-modules"><span class="abbr">CM</span><span class="label">Camera Modules</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/optical-sensors/mems-sensors"><span class="abbr">MS</span><span class="label">MEMS Sensors</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/optical-sensors/microdisplay"><span class="abbr">MD</span><span class="label">Microdisplay</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the module has to see or display and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Optical &amp; Sensors &middot; MEMS Sensors</div><h1 class="mk-h1">MEMS sensor assembly</h1><p class="mk-lede">A MEMS die is a mechanical structure, and an optical sensor die has to be reached by light. Neither tolerates a package that loads it or a line that leaves particles on it, so the attach material, the cure profile and the cleanliness of the environment are process decisions rather than packaging details.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-mems-sensors" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ MEMS Sensors &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-mems-sensors" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hana assembles MEMS and optical sensor devices on cleanroom lines under controlled ESD handling, using low-stress die attach and cavity or clear package formats matched to the device. Sensor and MEMS packaging has run inside our OSAT operations for years, on the same floors as our IC assembly and optical work.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Optical sensor packages</span></div><div class="desc">proximity, ambient light, color and time-of-flight sensor devices, assembled and packaged as finished sensor components.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">MEMS die assembly</span></div><div class="desc">MEMS die attached, interconnected and packaged, with the attach method chosen to keep mechanical stress off the structure.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Cavity and clear packages</span></div><div class="desc">clear transfer mold, metal and plastic caps, and film-assist mold, selected per device rather than applied as a standard format.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Cleanroom build and test coverage</span></div><div class="desc">assembly under controlled ESD handling, with electrical and functional test available to the program's requirements.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Process depth sits on the capability page: MEMS &amp; Sensor Assembly owns the wafer-level handling and probe steps that run ahead of packaging, and the attach methods matched to each device.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/microelectronic-assembly/mems-sensor-assembly">Explore MEMS &amp; Sensor Assembly <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Holding a die without loading it</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Two things decide whether a sensor assembly yields: how much stress the package puts into the die, and how clean the die stayed on the way there. Hana works both as process. Low-stress die attach — material and cure profile selected for the device rather than for throughput — keeps the package from bearing on a moving MEMS structure. Cavity and clear formats give an optical die the space or the light path it needs without adding a second alignment problem. And because a single particle or static discharge on an exposed sensor die is a scrapped unit, assembly runs on cleanroom lines under controlled ESD handling from die through to sealed package.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ayutthaya"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Ayutthaya</div><div class="note">MEMS and optical sensor assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ohio"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">USA</span></span><div class="nm">Ohio</div><div class="note">optical and precision assembly</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/lamphun"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">Thailand</span></span><div class="nm">Lamphun</div><div class="note">board-level support</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What MEMS device types can Hana assemble?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">MEMS die and optical sensor devices — proximity, ambient light, color and time-of-flight sensors among them — assembled and packaged as finished components. The device list is confirmed per program and per site.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Why does packaging stress matter for a MEMS sensor?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">A MEMS die is a mechanical structure, so force put into it by the die attach or the molding step does not stop at the package. Low-stress attach materials and cavity packaging are how Hana keeps the package from bearing on the die during build.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Can Hana test and calibrate sensors during production?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Electrical and functional test can be built into the line, and the test and calibration set is defined per program rather than assumed. Tell us what has to be verified before the part ships and we will confirm what runs in-house.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/optical-sensors" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Optical &amp; Sensors market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your MEMS or optical sensor program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>
